    <item>
      <title></title>
      <link>/authors/admin/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>/authors/admin/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;I am a compiler engineer at GlobalFoundries, working on &lt;a href=&#34;https://mips.com/processor-solutions/asip-designer/&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34;&gt;ASIP Designer&amp;rsquo;s&lt;/a&gt; extensively customized LLVM/Clang-based C/C++ compiler. My work spans the Clang front end, LLVM middle end, and custom backend tooling, with most of my work focused on analyses, transformations, and optimization-pipeline support. I am particularly interested in alias and memory-dependence analysis, code-restructuring transformations, and optimizations that take advantage of processor architecture.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Before joining GlobalFoundries, I worked on the same ASIP compiler technology at Synopsys until the business transferred in June 2026. The compiler dynamically supports processor targets generated from architecture descriptions, including RISC-V-based processors and highly specialized DSP architectures.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I completed my PhD at &lt;a href=&#34;https://www.tudelft.nl/en/&#34; target=&#34;_blank&#34;&gt;Delft University of Technology&lt;/a&gt; in 2023. My research focused on programmer-friendly intermittent computing and combined compiler transformations, processor architecture, and embedded systems. This work resulted in publications at PLDI, ASPLOS, and UbiComp.&lt;/p&gt;
</description>
